thank you very much for joining us i'm  john langler for the first time in  nearly a year  elementary schools across the valley  have children on campus  today marks the first step by clark  county school district to get all of its  students in class during the pandemic we  have team coverage for you this  afternoon bianca holman caught up with  parents  as they adjust to hybrid learning but we  start with hector mejia with a midday  update from superintendent dr jesus jara  hector  hey there and the superintendent said he  wants every parent to know that they  are following the recommendations made  by the cdc and the southern nevada  health district inside and outside the  classroom  this is wengert elementary school in the  east valley where the principal tells us  just about 37 percent of their students  chose to return to campus for hybrid  learning  that turns out to about 121 students in  total  the principal added they have an  additional 30 minutes of instruction  here to help students who may need to  catch up  ccisd has previously reported a slump in  grades across the district during  full-time distance learning  and earlier in the morning ccsd held an  event with superintendent dr  jesus jarrah along with state  superintendent joan ebert  as kids in grades pre-k through third  returned for the first time in almost a  year  a lot of excitement one mother told us  the biggest challenge was learning the  online system  vanessa rodriguez says she had to  shuffle her  work schedule around to teach her second  grader how to read  i'm excited for him i mean this is just  the first step but  i mean we're getting closer so hopefully  it returns back to normal soon  i talked to him and let him know mask on  all the time you know follow the rules  and  that way everything could just proceed  to normal it's going to be a challenge  i'm going to have half my class virtual  and then half my class in front of me at  the same time so i'm expecting that to  be a little bit of a challenge  ccsd is operating about 1600 bus routes  buses will only run at half capacity  that's about 28 students on board  students will be paid spaced out while  riding and drivers will  load buses from back to the front and  then students  will get off front to back to avoid too  much crossover so  be sure to watch out for students as  they walk to school or  as they walk home once the bell rings  reporting in the east valley hector  mejia  8 news now
 

